From a23432a5298cce1e7f8809a12aeaf95522902c50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mrinohk <5554998+Mrinohk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:37:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 17/31] mtp : optional reduced draft vocabulary for the
 Qwen3.5/3.6 MoE draft head

LLAMA_MTP_DRAFT_VOCAB=<file of int32 token ids> makes the MTP draft head compute logits only for
those tokens plus up to 4096 tokens seen in the current sequence; all other tokens get -inf.
The rows are copied from the LM head at load time into a buffer next to it (32k list: 78 MiB).
The target model and verification are unchanged, so it only changes which tokens are drafted.

On 2x P100 the draft head's full 248k-row LM head matvec was ~930 us per draft step (11% of
MTP decode). 35B UD-Q4_K_XL, 8-prompt MTP bench, 2 reps each:
  greedy:            113.3 -> 121.4 t/s (+7.1%), acceptance 0.830 -> 0.782
  production sampler 108.7 -> 115.6 t/s (+6.3%)
16k/48k/64k lists: 117.2 / 120.3 / 119.2 t/s. Without the sequence tokens 32k gave only +3.8%.
Greedy text moves the same way MTP already does vs no-spec (batch-shape rounding): mean chars
matching no-spec 445 (base) vs 422 (this), per prompt both earlier and later.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
